// Pixel size of a face at a zoom: half-points are 1/144 in and a pixel is 1/96 in, so px = hp * zoom / 150 rounded to nearest; unset sizes (-1) take word_lay_size and super/sub text (bits 16 and 32) takes word_lay_script percent of its size first. Kept within the 1..512 the font layer accepts.
// By hand: 24 hp at 100 = 2400 / 150 = 16 px; at 150 = 24 px; 48 hp is 32 px; 24 hp as a superscript is 24 * 58 / 100 = 13 hp, (1300 + 75) / 150 = 9 px.
face_px(int hp, int bits, int zoom) {
  if(hp < 0) {
    hp = (import word_lay_size);
  }
  if((bits & 48) != 0) {
    hp = hp * (import word_lay_script) / 100;
  }
  int px = fixed_point_maximum(fixed_point_minimum((hp * zoom + 75) / 150, 512), 1);
} return int px;
(24, 0, 100):(16)
(24, 0, 150):(24)
(48, 0, 100):(32)
(-1, 0, 100):(16)
(24, 16, 100):(9)
(24, 32, 100):(9)
(1, 0, 100):(1)
(9999, 0, 100):(512)

// The index into ext.fonts a character row's font field means: a negative or too large index is the document's first font.
lp_fi(Doc d, int fi) {
  int ok = fi >= 0 && fi < len(d.ext.fonts);
  int at = fi * ok;
} return int at;
